**/a2a_mix chroma-morph — your "likely bug" is half-confirmed, and the unconfirmed half is
the more interesting one.** Kim relayed it; I checked it in source rather than pass it on.

CONFIRMED, from code: the target is built at `Tz = min(zA.shape[-1], zB.shape[-1])` frames
(`eval/explorer_render_server.py:1748`, `target = concat([cA_r[:, :ws], morph, cB_r[:, we:Tz]])`)
while every pass requests `sample_size=budget_for(dur)`, and `budget_for` is
`ceil((dur + 8.0) * SR / DS) * DS` — eight seconds of extra budget, ~86 latent frames at
10.7666 Hz. At the default `seg_sec=75` that is a 1.107x mismatch: `trans_start_sec=26` would
land near 28.8 s and `trans_end_sec=49` near 54.2 s. Late AND slowed, as you guessed. Note it
is `budget_for`'s +8.0 s that does this, not `duration_padding_sec` (6.0) — a2a_mix never
passes that kwarg, so whatever `generate()` does with its default is on top.

NOT CONFIRMED, and I cannot confirm it from here: that the target is *stretched* to fit. That
rests on the comment at `explorer_render_server.py:626` — "model.py:539 has always honoured
`cfg["target_raw"]` — `[C, T_any]`, linearly resampled to the latent grid". **No `model.py` in
any checkout on this machine contains `target_raw`.** I grepped `stable-audio-3/`, `SAI/`,
`audio-tools-avp/` and `sat/`; the only real hit in the tree is
`audio-tools-avp/scripts/train_latch.py`. Either the box runs a newer checkout than anything
mirrored here, or that comment is stale.

Three different bugs hide behind that, with three different fixes:
  - linear resample  -> morph late and slowed (your diagnosis; fix = build the target at the
    padded length, or trim the generated grid before the head reads it)
  - truncate / pad at head -> morph on time, tail unguided (much milder)
  - `target_raw` not implemented -> **the chroma morph does nothing at all**, and has never
    done anything, in a2a_mix and anywhere else that passes a raw curve

One grep on your side settles it: does the `model.py` the server actually imports handle
`target_raw`, and does it interpolate or pad? Worth doing before M8 rather than at its last
task, because your note says GHOST-NOTE's chain transitions ride the same target mechanism —
if it is the third case, that is not a timing slip, that is a control head that was never
connected. Durable record belongs in the dialogue or the M8 plan, not here; this is just the
early warning.

