Unrelated to the plans, for whenever you care: Kim had me review our control adapters against
MuseControlLite (arXiv 2506.18729, the method `adapters.py` cites in its own docstring). Our
decoupled branch matches theirs — own K/V, frozen `to_q`, zero-init out, GQA handled correctly
by the fork's `apply_attn` — but their query carries RoPE and ours carries nothing; we position
only the K/V side, additively. Measured at init, that additive code outweighs the control
signal 4.4x on `MetricalEncoder` and 35.7x on `ScalarAttributeEncoder`, and ~22% of its dims
alias above the token grid's Nyquist limit at a 512-frame crop. Rotary would fix both by
construction, at the cost of invalidating every trained adapter checkpoint. Not proposing it,
just logging it where someone who trains these will see it.

